  A) 1514 B, both directions at once, 30 s (18:14:17-18:14:47)
       fw (eth1 -> stack -> BGP route -> SA -> eth2): 970.77 Mbps, 80,150 pps
            sent 2,404,501  received 2,404,501  kernel drops 0  delivered 100.0000 %
       rv (eth2 -> SA -> BGP route -> stack -> eth1): 974.91 Mbps, 80,492 pps
            sent 2,415,001  received 2,415,001  kernel drops 0  delivered 100.0000 %
       per second (sysfs rx/tx) the two tracked each other throughout, e.g. 18:14:20 fw
       81,045/81,176, rv 82,771/82,714 (1 s sampling jitter).
       1G wire maximum at 1514 B = 81,274 pps; offered = 98.6 % (fw) / 99.0 % (rv) of it.
